        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Figure 4: UCI energy efficiency: a depth-four tbtree. The dendrogram exposes the hierarchical regime structure of the simulated buildings, with the deepest low-cost split separating the two overall-height levels. Bracket heights are the impurity costs at which each split was committed.</div>\n",
